    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Index Assessment In Vector Store\n\nOwned By: Diego Alvarez\nLast Updated: 09/23/2026\n\nReusable subworkflow that embeds a process assessment and indexes it in Qdrant, enabling semantic similarity search across previously evaluated processes.\n\n## Expected Flow\n1. ReceiveIndexingRequest: Execute Workflow Trigger; receives the assessment content plus sourceWorkflowId/sourceExecutionId for traceability\n2. GenerateAssessmentEmbedding: Generates a vector embedding from the task description and automation potential via the local embedding model\n3. UpsertAssessmentToQdrant: Inserts/updates the assessment vector and payload in the Qdrant collection\n4. SearchSimilarAssessments: Queries Qdrant for previously indexed assessments similar to the current one\n\n## Resiliency & Error Handling\n- Independent Failure Isolation: by the time this subworkflow runs, the assessment is already persisted in MongoDB — failures here degrade semantic search only, not core data integrity, so every branch reports as warning severity\n- Centralized Alerts: each step's Error branch calls the notifyError subworkflow (NotifyEmbeddingGenerationFailed, NotifyQdrantUpsertFailed, NotifySimilarSearchFailed) instead of duplicating Slack logic\n- Traceability: sourceWorkflowId/sourceExecutionId are forwarded from the parent workflow's trigger, so Slack alerts link back to the actual pipeline execution rather than this subworkflow's own run",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 1136,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1744,
        -848
      ],
      "id": "10884da2-2c59-4c2c-af3c-e20168e9cc48",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    }
